WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:03.220
- Well, I saw something
you posted about sauce?

00:00:03.220 --> 00:00:04.951
You rate things by sauce.

00:00:04.951 --> 00:00:06.617
- Yeah.
- So, what does that mean,

00:00:06.617 --> 00:00:09.000
and where did the
sauce-rating system come from?

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:10.800
- You know, it started with...

00:00:11.860 --> 00:00:14.430
I've been obviously with my
kids a ton during this break,

00:00:14.430 --> 00:00:17.550
and so I find myself
cooking a ton of meals.

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:18.383
- Yes.

00:00:18.383 --> 00:00:22.000
- Cooking meals for kids
is such a thankless gig.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:23.040
- Yeah.

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:24.610
They think you're like a short-order cook.

00:00:24.610 --> 00:00:26.620
I'm like, "Yeah, I can't
just whip that up, so."

00:00:26.620 --> 00:00:28.970
- As well as, I'll make things...

00:00:28.970 --> 00:00:31.370
Before had kids, I just
didn't cook very much.

00:00:31.370 --> 00:00:36.310
So, I'll make something
that is really solid,

00:00:36.310 --> 00:00:38.647
and their response will
be after a bite, like,

00:00:38.647 --> 00:00:40.670
"I'll take cereal instead."

00:00:40.670 --> 00:00:42.730
And so, we started...

00:00:42.730 --> 00:00:44.487
we've been watching a
lot of cooking shows,

00:00:44.487 --> 00:00:45.400
- Mm hmm.

00:00:45.400 --> 00:00:48.370
- and so my way of getting
cooking to work with my kids is

00:00:48.370 --> 00:00:50.010
rather than they're themselves

00:00:50.010 --> 00:00:51.340
when I present them the food,

00:00:51.340 --> 00:00:54.137
they're the judges on a cooking show.

00:00:54.137 --> 00:00:56.130
- Oh my gosh, you're clever!

00:00:56.130 --> 00:00:58.460
- Well, it makes it all of a
sudden they eat the whole meal,

00:00:58.460 --> 00:00:59.420
because they're a judge.

00:00:59.420 --> 00:01:02.460
So, they'll say like, "I like the texture,

00:01:02.460 --> 00:01:04.810
but I don't love the
cheese on the quesadilla,"

00:01:04.810 --> 00:01:06.560
and I'll be like, "Thank
you, judge. How about you?"

00:01:06.560 --> 00:01:08.884
And they'll have to take another
bite, and blah, blah, blah.

00:01:08.884 --> 00:01:13.884
We realized in doing this game,
we didn't have enough terms,

00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:15.860
'cause they're six, they're twins,

00:01:15.860 --> 00:01:17.240
so, their numbers aren't great.

00:01:17.240 --> 00:01:18.520
So, they would say like...

00:01:18.520 --> 00:01:20.200
I would say, "Out of 10, what is it?"

00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:21.916
And they'd be like "100 out of one."

00:01:21.916 --> 00:01:22.950
(Kelly laughs)

00:01:22.950 --> 00:01:24.410
No, that doesn't work.

00:01:24.410 --> 00:01:27.113
So, we created a sauce system.

00:01:27.113 --> 00:01:28.350
- "100 out of one."

00:01:28.350 --> 00:01:29.430
- And so we'd be like, "All right,

00:01:29.430 --> 00:01:31.150
so if you really like something,

00:01:31.150 --> 00:01:32.080
it's extra sauce.

00:01:32.080 --> 00:01:34.740
If you don't like it, the sauce was bad."

00:01:34.740 --> 00:01:36.110
And so that's how we've been doing it.

00:01:36.110 --> 00:01:37.158
And then, you know.

00:01:37.158 --> 00:01:39.760
- That's the most clever...

00:01:39.760 --> 00:01:41.290
like you should write a parenting book.

00:01:41.290 --> 00:01:44.360
'Cause, man, my son,
my four-year-old is...

00:01:44.360 --> 00:01:46.720
I can get my girl, my
six-year-old, to eat anything.

00:01:46.720 --> 00:01:49.290
Especially if I bribe with
some kind of treat afterwards.

00:01:49.290 --> 00:01:51.490
My son will stave.

00:01:51.490 --> 00:01:53.830
He will literally look me
in the eye and go, "Nope."

00:01:53.830 --> 00:01:55.120
- It's so tricky!

00:01:55.120 --> 00:01:56.688
(Kelly laughs)
- Like, okay.

00:01:56.688 --> 00:01:58.520
Anyway, so, I'm going to try this.

00:01:58.520 --> 00:01:59.353
That's what I'm gonna do.

00:01:59.353 --> 00:02:00.270
I don't know if he'll
get that at four yet,

00:02:00.270 --> 00:02:01.820
but maybe by the time he's six.

